      "source": "core_enhanced/src/authoring/trial.rs:1057-1164",
      "detail": "Initial cancellation, prefix application decode error, readiness rejection and repeated execution decode error are tested. No new public-wrapper test forces receipt-phase fuel/byte failure or final-acceptance cancellation and verifies both operation phase and preserved native diagnostic phase/site/position.",
      "minimal_followup": "Use controlled low-limit or cancellation injection at a reached prefix/ready/final-acceptance boundary, asserting cursor and original diagnostic; do not infer the boundary from a generic error code alone."
    },
    {
      "id": "TS034-L02",
      "source": "core_enhanced/src/authoring/trial.rs:1106-1164",
      "detail": "Partial simulation accepts a Run snapshot then fails unknown command decode. Preservation comparisons cover receipt strings, accepted work and input hash; they do not independently compare native provenance, mutable gameplay/RNG/continuation, copy quota, old trace owner, or exact A/B generation identity.",
      "minimal_followup": "Extend an existing real gameplay failure fixture through the public wrapper, using postfailure replay/current state and owned-prefix equivalence; no need to duplicate all private runtime tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "TS034-L03",
      "source": "core_enhanced/src/authoring/trial.rs:996-1164",
      "detail": "The tests call public methods from an internal cfg-test module with embedded fixtures. They are not standalone default-release privacy/borrow or external-pack consumer evidence, and do not exercise new session describe/explain delegates.",
      "minimal_followup": "Use targeted standalone positive and forbidden API/borrow consumers when the staged public view surface stabilizes."
    }
